   "id": "bava_metzia.112b.1",
   "daf": "112b",
   "sentenceId": 0,
   "he": "שָׂכִיר בִּזְמַנּוֹ נִשְׁבָּע וְנוֹטֵל וְכוּ׳. שָׂכִיר אַמַּאי תַּקִּינוּ לֵיה רַבָּנַן (לְמִשְׁתְּבַע) [דְּמִשְׁתְּבַע] וְשָׁקֵיל?",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: If «a hired laborer» requests payment «at» the proper «time» and the employer claims he already paid him, the laborer «takes an oath» that he did not receive his wages «and» then «receives» the wages from the employer. The Gemara asks: «Why» did «the Sages institute» for «a hired laborer,» who is the plaintiff, «to take an oath and receive» his wages, in opposition to the principle that in the case of a monetary dispute between two parties, the defendant takes an oath that he is not liable and thereby exempts himself from payment?"
  }
